															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ihp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1267048); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1267048&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607417798" alt="Ihp" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1267048)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ihp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1267048); return false;" >Ihp</a></span> <span class="odate time_1499801371 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">11 Jul 2017 19:29</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3190357">
									

<p>This has been in the works for a little while, well over two months, I think. And it's the first skip I've posted since the 3000 contest. Oliver in this is based off of a cat I owned of the same name, who vanished two years ago. This is dedicated to him, as sappy as that sounds.</p>
<p>This is set in the S &amp; C Plastics universe, and as far as I'm concerned, is canon within it. Dr. Pike, Dr. Mattings and Dr. West have all appeared in at least one tale in S &amp; C P, as has Agent Ewell. Dr. Kola is the only one I haven't written into the canon <em>yet</em>.</p>
<p>Special thanks to SunnyClockwork and all others that helped critique this (my brain's frazzled from heat and travel, so if you helped to critique this, tell me and I'll add you here.)</p>

